# Lightning Pose App git (lpa-dev workspace)

## `lightning-pose-app` (all changes)

Every change in **`lightning-pose-app/`** — code, scripts, CI, config, and docs (`README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `DEV.md`, `AGENTS.md`, etc.) — uses the same workflow:

- New short-lived branch from `origin/main`, then a PR into `main`. One branch per feature, bugfix, or doc bundle. Combining is fine when the changes touch the same part of the repo, and one PR may close several related issues (list each with `Closes #N`).
- Do not open PRs from `jmrfox/dev`.
- Do not `git push` to `main`.

## `lpa-dev` (this repo)

Jordan is the only user. Work on **`main`** — no feature branches or PRs for `lpa-dev` (`feature_plans/`, `BUGS.md`, `.cursor/rules/`, scripts, etc.). That is separate from **`lightning-pose-app`**, which always uses branch + PR.

When Jordan asks for an lpa-dev change, make it, then commit and push to `main`. Commit only the files that change touched; leave unrelated work in the tree alone.

## Mentions

Don't @-mention people in issues, PRs, or comments unless they need to act or answer. To cite someone, use their name without the @ and link the comment.

## Changes that reach LP

- An LPA issue that needs a change in the **lightning-pose** repo gets the `LP change` label. LP is developed by others; open the LP side as its own PR there.
- When an LPA change makes something in the LP docs wrong or incomplete (install steps, app how-tos, screenshots), say so in the LPA PR description. Updating the LP docs with LPA information is ongoing work and does not need its own issue.

## App version

A pull request that changes Lightning Pose App **code** also updates the app version on that same branch before the PR is opened. A docs- or release-only PR follows the version/changelog/README rules below without unrelated code changes.

- Canonical version: `lightning-pose-app/app_server/pyproject.toml`, `[project].version`.
- Between releases, the version is the next app increment plus `.dev0` (after `X.Y.Z.W` ships, `X.Y.Z.(W+1).dev0`). If `main` already has a `.dev0` version, leave it and add to that changelog heading. Details are in `lightning-pose-app/DEV.md` under Version numbers.
- Add or extend `### [X.Y.Z.W.dev0]` at the top of `lightning-pose-app/CHANGELOG.md`. Name the test that covers each behavior change.
- Update the **Changelog** section in `lightning-pose-app/README.md`: keep **Latest release (PyPI)** on the last published version until a release ships; set **Development on `main`** to the current `[project].version` and link to the matching changelog heading. When cutting a release, bump the latest-release line to the new `X.Y.Z.W` section.
- Do not drop `.dev0`, and do not run `./scripts/publish_github_release.sh`, unless asked to cut a release.

## Commits in general

- Commit, push, open, merge, or close PRs **only when asked**.
- Do not run `./scripts/publish_github_release.sh` unless asked.
